# Cabinet theme

The shell of both cabinets is the purchased Threatrix template. The sidebar, header, cards, charts, and tables are already in this Next.js application. Do not put the archive back in the repository.

- Do not start a second application. Do not run the Vite template or `Ready_To_Deploy`. Do not put the archive in the cabinet image.
- Do not draw a separate dark shell beside Threatrix. A new cabinet screen repeats the Threatrix grid, spacing, glass, and color.
- The public site and the blog stay on the dark site theme.
- Data comes only from the Ledgesec journal. Do not connect the template's demo numbers or demo screens: attack map, threat feed, incidents, vulnerabilities, endpoints, CPU, EPS, MTTD, MTTR, plans, analyst roles, blocked-threat counter.
- Buttons, fields, dialogs, and menus stay shadcn. Color and frame come from Threatrix. Do not connect a second component library.
